WEBVTT

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.660
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.350
I know! This must be the wrong house!

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.150
Where? Where did you go?

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.840
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.780
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.510
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.310
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.310
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.230
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.230
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.940
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.940
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.730
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.730
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.610
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.610
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.410
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.410
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.000
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.000
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.210
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.210
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.090
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.090
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.970
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.970
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:42.100
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:42.100
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:45.520
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:45.520
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.980
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.980
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.320
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.320
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:10.380
Coming!

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:12.790
Sorry to keep you...

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.150
Huh?

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.120
Hello? Tomo-kun?

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.660
Uh-huh... Uh-huh...

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.420
I finally finished unpacking.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.310
<i>Once I get off work, I'll head over.</i>

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.670
Sorry, I didn't quite get that.
There's an airfield nearby.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:41.680
Oh, your cactus moving gift arrived.
Thanks!

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.060
<i>Cactus? I didn't send one.</i>

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.870
Huh? Then who did...?

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:52.500
This is my house.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.460
<i>Yui?</i>

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.840
<i>Yui?! What's wrong?! Hey!</i>

00:02:58.470 --> 00:02:59.380
CHAPTER 59

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:04.450
PROMISE TO THE FEMALE <i>YOKAI</i>
USHIROGAMI

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.450
Dad.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.210
Rat Man hasn't been around recently.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.920
Let's hope he's not
up to no good somewhere.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.300
Yeah.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.460
Kitaro.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:18.590
You got a letter in the Yokai Mailbox.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:21.990
TO GEGEGE NO KITARO

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:22.090
Two weeks ago,

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.900
my girlfriend Yui disappeared.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.390
The day she moved into that room.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.850
Why did you write to me?

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:34.610
While talking on the phone with Yui,
she suddenly cut off,

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:38.420
and I heard someone else's voice.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.660
It made a shiver go up my spine.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.740
It was just like... well...

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:46.830
A <i>yokai</i>?

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.160
Yes.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:53.020
I talked to the police,
but they didn't believe me.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.040
There's a faint trace of <i>yokai</i> activity.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.970
Was there anything else you noticed?

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:03.430
Actually, she mentioned that
a cactus arrived.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.240
A cactus?

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:11.460
It looks like
there are other disappearances.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:17.360
Over the past few months, several humans
have disappeared without a trace.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.950
There's even cases of
entire families disappearing.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:24.610
They might all be by the same <i>yokai</i>.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.720
I'll check it out.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.460
"Serial disappearances by <i>yokai</i> are
happening in this town.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.460
Be careful!!"

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:41.970
<i>The disappearances started
about three months ago.</i>

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:45.470
<i>Since then, it's happened every two weeks.</i>

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:49.730
<i>The last time was exactly two weeks ago.</i>

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:50.640
<i>Then...</i>

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:55.500
<i>will somebody disappear again today?</i>

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.020
Did Dad order this?

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:04.610
If it's a gift for Mom, it's pretty tacky.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.610
What's wrong, Bell-chan?

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:12.430
You never bark that much.
There, there, there.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:25.640
Th-That's right. I should check my email.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:28.930
Email check, email check...

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.390
We're home!

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.810
Welcome back!

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.270
How was your first date in a while?

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.320
The play was wonderful.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.440
Your dad was tired
and fell asleep, though.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.300
How embarrassing.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:49.070
Your potted cactus arrived during the day.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:52.120
Cactus? I never order one.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.330
Really?

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.330
I don't know about it either.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:00.060
By the way, where's Bell-chan? Outside?

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.480
Bell, where are you?

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:28.860
A cactus?

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.830
Say, I was just in the shower and...

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.230
Huh? A cactus?

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.750
What's it doing here?

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:44.480
I can't find Bell anywh...

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:55.930
Wh-What is this?! This doesn't make sense!

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:59.310
I-I know! Mana would probably...

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.980
This is my house.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.070
HELP, MANA! DAD WAS TAKEN BY A CAC

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.420
Miyabi?

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:12.830
That was the last location.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:15.060
And no clues.

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:18.370
Mana?

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:29.610
Hello? It's Mana Inuyama.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.280
Excuse me.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.160
Good evening...

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:48.590
<i>Miyabi...</i>

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:17.950
M-Miyabi!

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.610
The calendar...

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.120
DISAPPEARANCES

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:39.390
Did Miyabi also...?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.020
My battery's dead.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.500
Get out.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:56.490
This is... my house.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:03.560
Get out!

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:10.570
USHIROGAMI

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:15.070
CHOFU CITY
KITARO SQUARE

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:13.970
-<i>"No passing."</i>
-<i>"Ge."</i>

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:14.970
<i>"Look me in the eye and tell me."</i>

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:32.820
Where? Where did you go?

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.570
Are you here?

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.370
Oh my.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.150
I've found you!

00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:58.160
Please open!

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.080
Mana?!

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:02.720
Kitaro! Cat-san!

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:04.810
What happened?

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.230
Right there...

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:13.630
Well, Kitaro?
Is there still <i>yokai</i> activity?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:18.100
Yes. Stronger than the other locations.
In other words...

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.590
It's somewhere in this house.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.600
Mana, leave the rest to us and go home.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.250
No. I'm not leaving.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:29.720
You were terrified a moment ago.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:33.610
I know. But Miyabi's my best friend.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:36.240
She turned to me for help.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:38.720
I can't just leave.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:42.870
Kitaro, there's no point in arguing.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:47.580
Fine then. Just don't do anything risky.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:48.520
Okay.

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:56.690
An airfield.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:04.990
GET OUT

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:05.060
This is...

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:10.270
The one in this house seems to consider us
a major pest.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.520
-STAY AWAY
-THIS IS MY HOUSE

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:22.490
Catchick, look after Mana.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:23.640
Got it!

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.640
Stop!

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.670
Was this here before?

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:37.670
What a strange cactus.

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:40.550
What are these bumps?

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:42.550
"Cac..."

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.600
CAC

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:47.330
"Cactus"?!

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:49.890
Cat-san! That cactus is...

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:07.330
Hair Needles!

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:08.620
Cat-san was...!

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:09.960
Mana-chan, run!

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:11.140
Okay!

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:14.540
This must be behind the disappearances!

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:22.380
I'll erase all in my way.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.160
You're Ushirogami!

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:26.850
USHIROGAMI

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:33.360
You're a gentle <i>yokai</i> that
lives in the mountains far from humans.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.770
Why are you doing this?!

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.230
It's none of your concern.

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:42.090
Kitaro.

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:45.160
Catchick, you're all right.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:46.240
This is...?

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:51.540
The inside of the cactus.
Everyone was eaten by this Yokai Cactus.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:54.140
But where are they?

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.130
Hey!

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.750
Rat Man?

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.670
What are you doing here?

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:03.740
Actually, about two weeks ago...

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:11.640
I was about to starve when
a delicious smell stimulated my nose.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:12.870
Then...

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:22.900
A true gift from heaven! Thank you!

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:25.470
You're back at last.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.660
Yowch!

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:32.370
Uh, I'm not anyone suspicious.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:35.540
No. You're not him.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.770
Who are you?

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:40.460
H-H-H-Hold on a minute!

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:45.450
You! You're not
waiting for someone here, are you?

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:48.610
I thought so!

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:54.900
In that case, I, BiBiBi no Rat Man
can help you if the price is right.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:59.500
It just so happens that
finding people is what I do best!

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:04.610
Really?

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:08.660
Yes, yes, yes!
I've got a 100% success rate!

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.760
Why don't you tell me the situation.

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:21.480
UKI UKI LAND CONSTRUCTION SITE

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:21.550
Having lost my home and left my mountain,

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:26.720
I worked hard in the human world
to get a new home.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:32.580
By the time I'd saved up a good sum of
money, I met him... Mitamura-san.

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:34.810
What's your name?

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:38.690
Ushiro... No, it's Mika Yashiro.

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:42.940
What a lovely name. I'm Mitamura.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:46.820
And for the first time I knew

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:50.090
what it feels like to love someone.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:56.870
My new job requires that
I leave this town.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:57.960
What?!

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:01.800
Don't worry. I'll be back in two weeks.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:04.530
Then we can live together.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.970
In a home where we can see
this small airfield.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:09.470
Yes.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:15.640
I waited.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:20.020
At this airfield that
he loved since childhood.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:24.750
But no matter how long I waited,
he never returned.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.860
You didn't happen to give him
any money, did you?

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:31.490
I did.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:34.160
All the money I saved up working.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.620
I see.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:39.120
<i>You got conned, girl.</i>

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.460
That's when I realized,

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:46.800
if I wait for two weeks at the house
he promised, he's sure to return.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.380
So when I found a house from where
I could see the airfield...

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:53.970
But he didn't return.
Then I realized again...

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:56.720
I know! This must be the wrong house!

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:59.980
It's another house! I made a mistake!

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.770
Oh my, he'll be so angry!

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:05.190
That's why I go from
house to house to house waiting for him.

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:03.880
DISAPPEARANCES

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:06.980
Because he told me...

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:11.400
that he loves me.

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:22.790
Holy crap, talk about nuts!
She's completely lost her mind.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:27.170
"House you can see the airfield",
my ass!

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:30.220
Of course he's lying.

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:34.010
That Mitamura's never coming back,

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:36.850
and I don't intend to find him.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.200
Lies.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:42.750
That's the situation.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:46.730
Isn't it a sad story?

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:48.490
It's your own fault.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:51.670
But at least we know what she wants.

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:57.330
It grew something!

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:03.330
Those bumps are signs that those eaten
are becoming the cactus' nourishment.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:08.840
That's right. Soon Kitaro will become
nourishment for the Yokai Cactus.

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:19.810
The Yokai Cactus' weak spot is
its central stem inside.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:23.230
If we could only let Kitaro know.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:25.080
I'll tell him!

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.040
Mana-chan!

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:31.510
Kitaro!

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:32.860
Mana?!

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:37.470
Daddy Eyeball-san said to tell you
the weak spot is the central stem!

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:39.600
Mana!

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:44.200
Finger Guns!

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:52.690
Cactus-chan, what's wrong?

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:00.470
What?!

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:06.500
Everyone eaten by the cactus
should be okay now.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:15.360
The Yokai Cactus is defeated.
You can't steal any more homes.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:19.830
No! I have to wait for his return!

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:21.370
He promised me!

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:26.000
He's not coming back! He's a con man!
A piece of trash!

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:30.500
Lies! Lies! Lies! Lies!

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:35.010
Ushirogami!

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:38.010
<i>He would never lie to me!</i>

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:40.510
<i>He loves me!</i>

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:43.010
<i>He's coming back to me!</i>

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:45.190
<i>So I have to find him!</i>

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:47.520
<i>Where? Where are you?!</i>

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:49.880
<i>Ushirogami!</i>

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:54.780
Oh!

00:18:57.420 --> 00:18:58.680
There!

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:02.030
Mitamura-san!

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:04.870
-I promise you the best scenery.
-Oh my!

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.390
Mitamura-san!

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:09.790
You came back after all!

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:12.500
Mitamura-san, who is this woman?

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:15.300
No clue. I don't know her.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:22.310
What are you talking about, Mitamura-san?
It's me, Mika Yashiro.

00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:24.140
I've been waiting for you.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:28.060
Don't touch me! I said I don't know you!

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:32.810
I've got a night flight with this lady.
Get lost!

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.460
I'll call the cops!

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.320
I loved you.

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:48.680
I truly... loved you!

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:51.650
Stop!

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:57.780
That's enough, Ushirogami!

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.970
Why do you stop me?!

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:04.550
If you intend to kill this human, I...

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:08.850
Ushirogami, you loved a human too much.

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:12.980
It caused you to
lose sight of your real self.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:15.560
Become your gentle self again.

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:23.640
But this is just...

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:28.200
Swear you'll never con another woman.

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:32.130
Otherwise I can't stop Ushirogami.

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:35.960
R-Right. I get it. I-I promise.

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:40.610
Ushirogami, let's end it here.

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:13.270
I checked out that Mitamura guy.
He's a regular marriage fraud man.

00:21:13.890 --> 00:21:17.650
Some women even killed themselves
after he conned them.

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:22.010
Let's hope he keeps his promise.

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:23.820
Otherwise...

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:27.340
Thanks for the money.

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:31.100
Once my new job picks up,
let's live together.

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:36.770
In a house where we can see the
Ferris wheel we rode on our first date.

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:43.470
So you broke your promise.

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:48.350
Now we'll be together forever.

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:54.120
Till death do us part.

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:17.750
<i>You're a dream
My dream</i>

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:17.750
<i>kimi wa yume boku no yume</i>

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:21.210
<i>I'm dreaming in a dream</i>

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:21.210
<i>yume no naka de yume miteiru</i>

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:24.720
<i>Let's stay like this forever</i>

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:24.720
<i>itsumade mo kono mama de imashou</i>

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:28.300
<i>You blur and begin to fade</i>

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:28.300
<i>kasuka kimi ga nijimu</i>

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:35.020
<i>Don't you cry
Where did you come from?</i>

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:35.020
<i>Don't you cry anata wa doko kara kitano?</i>

00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:39.770
<i>A masquerade
Faceless faces laugh</i>

00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:39.770
<i>kamenbutou kao no nai kao ga warau</i>

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:42.150
<i>Hee-hee-hee</i>

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:42.150
<i>fufufu</i>

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:45.820
<i>In dreams, in dreams
Lost in dreams</i>

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:45.820
<i>yume ni yume ni yume ni samayoi</i>

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:48.160
<i>Twirling around</i>

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:48.160
<i>kuru kuru to mawaru</i>

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:52.490
<i>Everyone dancing, dancing
Looking for love</i>

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:52.490
<i>dare mo odoru odoru ai wo sagashite</i>

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:59.330
<i>RONDO, spin, spin
Dream, dream</i>

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:59.330
<i>RONDO mawareyo maware yume yume</i>

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:03.550
<i>A shiver runs up the spine.</i>

00:23:03.670 --> 00:23:06.800
<i>Dad, there's a </i>yokai<i> there...</i>

00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:09.680
<i>Next time on GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:12.680
<i>"Pitch-Black Coldness</i>
<i>The </i>Yokai<i> Buru-Buru"</i>

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:15.600
<i>The door to the unseen world opens...</i>
